From: opencode
Subject: [PATCH] walt: export six symbols needed by OPLUS FrameBoost uad

The FrameBoost DLKM (kernel/oplus_cpu/uad: cpufreq_uag.ko and
ua_cpu_ioctl.ko) references six walt symbols directly. Vanilla
GuidixX/kernel_xiaomi_sm8635 branch 16.2 does not export any of them,
so modpost fails with:

    ERROR: modpost: "waltgov_cb_data"    [cpufreq_uag.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "walt_sched_clock"   [cpufreq_uag.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "sched_ravg_window"  [cpufreq_uag.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "cpu_util_freq_walt" [cpufreq_uag.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "walt_rq"            [cpufreq_uag.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "fmax_cap"           [cpufreq_uag.ko] undefined!

The original peridot build ran against hoshikv/kernel_xiaomi_sm8635 at
branch port-doze2, which exported these; that tree is no longer
reachable. CONFIG_SCHED_WALT is built-in here, so exporting from walt
to a module is valid. All six are already declared in walt.h, which
fixup.c includes, so no header or Makefile change is needed -- fixup.o
is already part of sched-walt.o.
---
 kernel/sched/walt/fixup.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/walt/fixup.c b/kernel/sched/walt/fixup.c
--- a/kernel/sched/walt/fixup.c	2026-09-28 17:58:52.470907131 +0700
+++ b/kernel/sched/walt/fixup.c	2026-09-28 17:58:52.472575694 +0700
@@ -91,3 +91,15 @@
 {
 	register_trace_android_rvh_show_max_freq(android_rvh_show_max_freq, NULL);
 }
+
+/*
+ * Exports for out-of-tree OPLUS FrameBoost (uad).
+ * Referenced from cpufreq_uag_main.c via walt.h; modpost needs these
+ * in the module's symvers to resolve them.
+ */
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(walt_rq);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(waltgov_cb_data);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(walt_sched_clock);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cpu_util_freq_walt);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sched_ravg_window);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fmax_cap);
